CHAR definitions {"directness":"per record: drawn-path length (points[0],points[1] polyline) over the straight-line distance between the record's own first and last drawn anchor; records shorter than 1 cell-width are dropped","elevProfile":"mean h of the record's land cells (h>=20) against the mean h of the direct-corridor cells, where the corridor is every cell within 1.5 cell-widths of the record's own direct segment (sampled every half cell-width) and the land mean is the whole map's land cells","crestHit":"for records whose direct corridor holds a cell with h>=50 (the crossing set): crestSag is the corridor's highest h minus the record's own highest h, and a hit is a sag of at most 10 — the record came up to the crest instead of bending around it. The sag is the primary reading: a distance radius on the crest cell cannot separate reach from a detour, because the corridor's own width puts the crest near any chain that stays on the line","biomeShare":"share of the record set's distinct land cells in each biome, against that biome's share of all land cells","passUnder":"distinct tunnel cells that are surface-only burg cells (burg with ground-level presence and no below-level presence) — the F7.2 audit definition","nearMiss":"distinct tunnel cells that are not surface-only burg cells but have such a burg cell among their neighbours","anchorMinDist":"per record, the smallest distance (in cell-widths) from any drawn point to any surface-only burg dot; the mean over records is reported"}
